{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>The voice of YHWH hews flames of fire.</b> Rabbi Moses said: this is a hint to the stone that is like iron, burning. And the meaning of חוצב is that it hews them from the flint, and the meaning is by analogy, as though it hewed them. And in my opinion: the meaning concerns the lightnings, in the manner of: \"And the Most High utters His voice, and after it He sends His arrows\" [Job 36:32 — the verse reads קולו / חציו]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "Resolved the unmarked biblical quotation by comparison with Job 36:32, whose wording matches exactly."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:53.109676258Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}